OK md:416 corpus/knowledge/intake-and-finalize.md:78-92  [For every `claims/<id>/<slug>/status.json` it then: ⏎  ⏎ 1. **Filters**: skip `state !== 'DONE'`; skip verdict matching ⏎ `/not.claimable/i` (review-overturned); skip any `disposition` field ⏎ (held/shelved by decree); skip `submission_state === 'DISCLOSED_FREE'` ⏎ (VDP freebies are never claim-ready). ⏎ 2. **Re-validates**: fresh `~/Projects/the-bounty-hunter/ops/claim-check.mjs` run per package; nonze ⏎ `claim_rejected` telemetry (stdout tail 300 chars), `rejected++`. ⏎ 3. **Commits**: `git add` the package; if staged diff non-empty → ⏎ `commit -m "claim(<id>): accept <slug>"`; if clean → reuse last commit ⏎ touching the path. No commit containing the bytes → `claim_commit_failed`. ⏎ 4. **Byte-proofs the tag target**: `git diff --quiet <sha> -- <pkg>` must be ⏎ clean — the tag must point at bytes equal to what's on disk. ⏎ 5. **Tags**: `claim-ready/<id>/<slug>`. Existing tag on the SAME sha → reuse; ⏎ existing tag on a DIFFERENT sha → `claim_tag_conflict`, rejected, never]
